// gen-skin: draws every sprite of the Pyxamp face into face/assets/skin.png and
// writes its index to face/lib/sprites.js.
//
// The pixels come from the approved mock's own pixel maps and primitives
// (docs/mock/skin.js), run here against an in-memory raster, and from the
// W95FA Grid font (docs/mock/fonts/W95FAGrid.ttf), rasterised at one font
// pixel per skin pixel. No Nullsoft or Webamp bitmap is read.
//
// Usage: face/tools/gen-skin           write both files
//        face/tools/gen-skin --check   exit 1 when the committed files differ
//
// Node is used because the source of truth (skin.js) is JavaScript: running it
// keeps the pixel maps in one place instead of a transcription.
